        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173-a1-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0382" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg362"/>

                <p rendition="#center">[Enclosed with No 1.]</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Affidavit of Robert Devine.</hi></p>
                <p>I hereby declare that I have this day been shipped by and before Mr. Black, to
                    join some confederate vessel now in the offing, to proceed to Wilmington. I
                    signed articles, but the name of the vessel was not filled in. Some eighty or
                    ninety other persons have also shipped for the same vessel. I was told by Mr.
                    Black that he wanted no man who could not fight, or who was afraid of gunpowder,
                    as they would have to fight their way to Wilmington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT DEVINE.</signed></closer>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Delivered before me <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-06">this 6th October,
                        1864</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>W. C. J. HYLAND, <hi rendition="#italic">J. P.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
